<title>USA: Oregon $30 mln housing bonds repriced, yields cut. [CORRECTED 22:47 GMT]</title>
<headline>Oregon $30 mln housing bonds repriced, yields cut. [CORRECTED 22:47 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bear, Stearns &amp; Co. said Tuesday it repriced Oregon's $29.8 million mortgage revenue bond deal, lowering yields in several maturities and leaving the top yield in 2027 unchanged at 6.20 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>STATE OF OREGON</p>
<p>HOUSING AND COMMUNITY SERVICES DEPARTMENT</p>
<p>RE: $29,750,000*</p>
<p>MORTGAGE REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>(SINGLE-FAMILY MORTGAGE PROGRAM)</p>
<p>1997 SERIES A AND</p>
<p>1997 SERIES B (FEDERALLY TAXABLE)</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
